&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Professional Services organization at Miro is focused on ensuring our Enterprise customers achieve exceptional outcomes through the Innovation Workspace. Our team of strategic advisors, implementation experts, and forward deployed consultants work side-by-side with customers to transform how they collaborate, build, and innovate—powered by agentic AI and Miro&#39;s world-class platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Forward Deployed Consultant, Manufacturing, you will apply AI solutions to transform and automate the core operating processes of leading industrial enterprises. You will engage directly with C-level executives, help them identify high-impact opportunities, build and test enterprise-grade AI solutions on their own data and systems, and drive measurable business outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits at the intersection of strategy, operations, and technology. You will be paired with an Account Executive against named accounts—hunting for problems worth solving, then proving they can be solved. Generalist FDCs lead client discussions across industries; as the Manufacturing Specialist, you are the dedicated depth they bring in when a pursuit turns on industrial expertise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Agenda:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with senior executives—COO, Chief Supply Chain Officer, Chief Digital Officer, VP Manufacturing, VP Quality—to define an AI transformation agenda Miro can attach to&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the initial CxO conversation that creates awareness of what AI makes possible for the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualify opportunities before committing to a Validation Sprint: sponsor authority, commitment, and the account&#39;s potential to become a multi-year, seven-figure relationship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Validation Sprints:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Co-author the Sprint charter with the AE: the business problem, its value, our approach, exit criteria, and the partnership proposal that follows success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the Sprint end to end—immerse, prioritise, build, read out—developing and testing the solution on the customer&#39;s real data and systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take manufacturing processes apart and rebuild them on AI-first principles across five workflows: new product development and gate review, quality and continuous improvement, portfolio and program management, operations and launch readiness, and process development and transformation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build using Miro&#39;s AI Workflows, Prototypes, and Goals, Roadmaps &amp;amp; Delivery capabilities, extended through Miro&#39;s API, WebSDK, and MCP integrations into ERP, PLM, MES, and quality systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Value and Conversion:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn Sprint outcomes into a business value story, ROI model, and KPI baseline—grounded in metrics the customer already runs on: gate cycle time, requirement coverage at gate, defect recurrence, cost of poor quality, capacity utilisation, on-time launch rate, ramp-to-full-rate time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support executive leadership in delivering the Value Story read-out to the sponsor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Co-own with the AE the conversion of Sprint outcomes into the partnership proposal and commercial approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the scope of Professional Services involvement post-sale and hand over cleanly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Package what you learn and radiate it—internally to Sales, Marketing, and Product, and externally through thought leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll need&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years in &lt;strong&gt;top-tier consulting, for

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Sony Interactive Entertainment?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sony Interactive Entertainment isn’t just the Best Place to Play — it’s also the Best Place to Work. Sony Interactive Entertainment (SIE) is the company behind the PlayStation brand. As a subsidiary of Sony Group Corporation, we’re part of a proud legacy of innovation and excellence. SIE is a dynamic technology company, delivering cutting-edge hardware and network services to more than 100 million people and an entertainment leader, home to some of the most beloved and recognizable intellectual properties (IP) in the world. Our role at SIE is to create and nurture the experiences under the PlayStation brand, a name synonymous with entertainment excellence and creativity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;PlayStation Studios is the game development division of Sony PlayStation and is responsible for developing some of the most recognisable and ambitious console games and franchises on PlayStation, including The Last of Us, Horizon, Spider-Man, God of War, Helldivers and Gran Turismo.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We work with some of the best game studios in the world, and use data to help them make their games even better. We provide end-to-end analytics services for PlayStation Studios and use data to help them in the game development lifecycle. We are looking for talented people to join us in pushing the boundaries of game analytics for PlayStation games.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role offers a flexible hybrid working arrangement, with most time spent working remotely unless you prefer to come into the office. We attend the office for key moments that matter, such as important team meetings, collaboration sessions and business activities where in-person engagement is beneficial.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Role Overview:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Lead Data Engineer, you’ll work in our cross-disciplinary Data Platform team to ingest and process high-volume data.&amp;nbsp; You’ll work closely with our Game Analytics analysts and analytics engineers, who use this data to gain valuable insights both during game development and post-launch.&amp;nbsp; As a lead, you’ll scale our platform and help us define its technical direction, expand its reach, and help define and build the future of analytics for PlayStation games.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;What you’ll be doing:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own parts of our pipeline, and drive improvements to achieve our technical and business goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build supporting services for our pipeline, for example working on integrations with in-game maps and video tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate our data collection platform and our BI tools to enable studio self-service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the Devops team, our analytics engineers, and stakeholders across the studio business group.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Focus on improving data quality, lineage and observability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support our existing tooling, improving quality and documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a technical expert and share than knowledge with your colleagues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;What we’re looking for:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience building and owning Data Pipelines for high-throughput streaming and batch data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are adept at writing code in Go or write Python with a willingness to learn Go.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are experienced in building robust, scalable, and resilient services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can demonstrate measurable impact that you have made in your current and previous roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy solving data problems, and can take responsibility for quality, investigations and remediation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cloud data services.&a

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Sony Interactive Entertainment?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
