&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Bristol, UK &lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Start date: &lt;/strong&gt;September 2027&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Application deadline&lt;/strong&gt;: Midnight, 29th November 2026&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;We encourage you to apply early, as we may close applications before the advertised deadline.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;The Graduate Programme at Graphcore&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join Graphcore in a permanent role and start your career with two years of hands-on learning. From day one, you’ll be trusted to take ownership, share your ideas and help shape what we’re creating. You’ll tackle challenging problems alongside a team who support your development and are as excited about your success as you are.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;iframe style=&quot;display: table; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/embed/sUqy-WuXPsE&quot; width=&quot;560&quot; height=&quot;314&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you’ll work on&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Put your technical foundations to work on the cloud platforms that help demanding AI workloads run at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Graduate Cloud Platform Engineer, you’ll help develop, deploy and operate services across Graphcore’s high-performance AI infrastructure. Your work will support the systems used by internal teams and Graphcore cloud customers. We believe technology should expand human potential and make progress more accessible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll write automation, investigate issues, analyse logs and metrics, and help validate AI hardware and the infrastructure around it. It’s a chance to see how Linux, networking, storage and cloud services fit together and contribute to the platforms that make large-scale AI possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;How you’ll learn and grow&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;During the two-year programme, you’ll build practical experience in Linux, cloud technologies, networking, storage, observability, OpenStack , Kubernetes, continuous integration and delivery (CI/CD), and Infrastructure-as-Code.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hands-on automation and troubleshooting will help you understand how these systems fit together and develop a methodical approach to investigating issues. You’ll learn to use logs and metrics to test your thinking and explain what you find.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working with engineers, researchers and Datacentre Operations will help you understand how platform decisions affect the people using these services and develop your technical judgement and communication skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, IT, Electronic Engineering or a related subject, completed by summer 2027 or within the two years before the programme starts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience using the Linux command line, with scripting or programming skills such as Python or Bash&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Git or another version-control system, with a clear approach to documentation and code review&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A methodical approach to troubleshooting and the ability to communicate your findings and work with others&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll be curious about cloud infrastructure, platform engineering or computer systems, with an interest in areas such as networking, storage, containers or observability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can demonstrate these skills through coursework, a dissertation, personal or team projects, open-source work, placements or other relevant experience. Tell us what you built or investigated, how you approached it and what you learned.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Benefits&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working: Balance your work and personal life with greater flexibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retirement planning support: Up to 5% matched pension&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Phantom equity: Share in Graphcore’s success&lt;/l

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About Zinier&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;80% of the workers across the globe are Deskless. These are the people who keep our lights on and gas flowing, build roads and bridges, run our manufacturing factories, ensure that we get healthcare service, and provide us with reliable phone and internet connectivity. As entrepreneurs, have we considered solving their problems and making them more productive?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zinier is a company on a mission to empower frontline workers - and the people supporting them - to achieve greater things for themselves and the world around them. With the majority of workers worldwide being deskless, Zinier recognizes the need for Technology Equity to improve the lives and productivity of these workers who keep the world up and running.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have global team headquartered in Silicon Valley, with a hybrid workforce across the United States, Canada, Europe, Latin America, Singapore, and Bangalore, India, with leading investors that include Accel, ICONIQ Capital, Founders Fund, Newfund Capital, NGP Capital, Tiger Global Management, and Qualcomm Ventures LLC.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re a Solution Architect with a proven track record of transforming complex technical requirements into well-structured, customer-centric solutions, we’d love to meet you. Experience in Field Service Management is a must, particularly in defining system specifications and identifying opportunities to optimize solutions. You should also bring experience working on business transformation programs where product-based solutions must be adapted and scaled to fit dynamic environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for people who thrive in agile, collaborative, global teams and who enjoy working with best-in-class technology to deliver meaningful impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with lead solution architects to gather and analyze business and technical requirements, define solution scope, and document processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate workshops, customer meetings, and design sessions to align stakeholders on solution design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with product, development, and cross-functional teams to design scalable, customer-aligned solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and maintain technical implementation documentation (e.g., Low-Level Designs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate, configure, and customize product features while ensuring integration and implementation best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot technical issues, propose solutions, and provide post-implementation support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute insights to continuously improve Zinier’s product roadmap and delivery methodology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6–12 years of SaaS experience in professional services or client-facing roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in Field Service Management (required).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in high-growth startups with evolving product roadmaps (preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creative problem-solving skills for addressing product gaps and business challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering solutions in an Agile environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with project management tools such as JIRA, Confluence, or equivalents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical knowledge of enterprise applications, workflows, integrations, and databases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of data models, JavaScript, and JSON.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication skills in English, with the ability to engage with stakeholders across diverse levels and backgrounds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High attention to detail, reliability, and follow-through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
