&lt;p data-pasted=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About SiTime&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SiTime Corporation is the precision timing company. Our semiconductor MEMS programmable solutions offer a rich feature set that enables customers to differentiate their products with higher performance, smaller size, lower power and better reliability. With more than 3 billion devices shipped, SiTime is changing the timing industry. For more information, visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globenewswire.com/Tracker?data=KZboO_E5KYNf2nXu9snYUrujcxPVV14r8VUqaw-krQjviK4SVzg-T3gX0Yv8pdrIU2yKG5VITW08WA-AWCTQKQ==&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;www.sitime.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join the team that is revolutionizing the timing industry with the best silicon Microelectromechanical Systems (MEMS) timing products in the world. As a Principal MEMS Development Engineer, you will use your technical and creative problem-solving skills to push forward MEMS technology and engineer resonators for SiTime’s next-generation timing products. It is not necessary to meet all job requirements to be a qualified candidate for the position.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul type=&quot;disc&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead definition and execution of challenging technical projects.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise management of challenges, impact, recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop new or improved resonators, MEMS technologies and/or products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design MEMS devices and characterize their electrical, mechanical, and thermal performance on wafer level and/or device level.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with process team to drive continuous improvement in MEMS yields.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extend and enhance automated infrastructure for MEMS design, measurements, and data analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and analyze experiments to understand device physics, materials, and fabrication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interface with local and overseas vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work in cross-functional teams, including circuits, systems, and packaging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working/supporting other projects as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications &amp;amp; Requirements: &amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ph.D. in ME, EE, Physics, or equivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 3 years of industry experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled scientist with ability to design, conduct, and analyze experiments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent problem identification and problem-solving abilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent knowledge of mechanics, electrodynamics, thermodynamics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge in fundamentals of MEMS devices physics and fabrication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with finite element simulation tools (COMSOL, ANSYS) and data processing tools (Matlab, Python).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent interpersonal, organizational, written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for delivering exceptional results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired Characteristics &amp;amp; Attributes:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul type=&quot;disc&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3 -10 years of industry experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intermediate to advanced knowledge of programing languages, circuits, metrology equipment and methods.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Statistical analysis and tools such as R or JMP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge in MEMS microfabrication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
